<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ronald Reagan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1911">1911</a>–<a href="/years/2004">2004</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ronald Reagan was the 40th president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, serving from 1981 to 1989, after careers as a film actor and governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>. He cut taxes, increased military spending and took a hard line against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, launching the Strategic Defense Initiative, but in his second term negotiated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-gorbachev">Mikhail Gorbachev</a> and signed the INF Treaty of 1987, which eliminated a whole class of nuclear missiles.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ronald-reagan.jpg" alt="Ronald Reagan" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michael Evans · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Official_Portrait_of_President_Reagan_1981.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
